 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling, punctuation and syllables: amo without its accent in bar 6 (sung and written in IPA as amò), fatto io (the libretto has fatt'io), Almagna (libretto Lamagna), the numbers as the print divides them (sei cento, due cento, trent' una, novant' una), cittadine with one t in bar 72 (cittadine in bar 40; both written in IPA as cittadine), di lodarla la gentilezza (the libretto has di lodar la gentilezza), e la grande maestosa (libretto è la grande), purchè in bar 143 and pur che in bar 154. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S08) and the IPA was checked against Castel. Leporello sings the catalogue (Allegro) twice, with the score's repeats of mille e tre and d'ogni forma, d'ogni età; in the Andante con moto he repeats e la grande maestosa, sings la piccina nine times, and ends with many repeats of voi sapete quel che fa. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
